  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "RTPS: fix negative participant_idx for RTPX messages",
  "description": "RTPX messages are always sent to PORT_BASE (7400) regardless of the\ndomain_id they advertise via PID_DOMAIN_ID. The existing formula:\n\n  doffset = destport - PORT_BASE - domain_id * DOMAIN_GAIN\n\nproduces a negative doffset (e.g. -2500 for domain 10) which causes\nparticipant_idx values like -130, -255, -1255, or -12505 to be shown\nin the \"Default port mapping\" section of the dissection tree.\n\nWhen the RTPS magic number is RTPX_MAGIC_NUMBER, force doffset to 0\nso the dissector displays MULTICAST_METATRAFFIC with the correct\ndomainId and no spurious participantIdx field.\n\nRegular RTPS captures are unaffected.\n\nAI-Assisted: yes (Copilot)",
  "state": "merged",
